@* Load-bearing, despite looking like boilerplate.

   A project with no .razor files at all is not treated as a Blazor project by the Razor
   SDK, so the Blazor framework static web assets — including _framework/blazor.server.js —
   are never contributed to it. The page then renders, MapBlazorHub answers on
   /_blazor/negotiate, and the component still never appears: the browser 404s on the
   script, so the circuit never starts.

   helsedata's Optimizely project satisfies this naturally; it has an _Imports.razor and
   thirteen .razor components of its own. A sample host with none was the anomaly. *@

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor
